## Context

The cost–quality Pareto frontier (Figure 2 in `slides/manuscript/main.md`,
line 21) and the Experiment 1 cost table are both half-built. The
caption claims the script does things the script does not do, the
caption's numbers are stale pilot data, the cost table renders as
LaTeX only and does not land in the manuscript, and the "quality"
axis covers only Accuracy of the four §2 dimensions. Surfaced during
0151 review (2026-05-21 conversation); not picked up by any earlier
ticket.

## Relevant files

- `src/aedist/plot_pareto.py` — scatter plot (no envelope, no family
  colouring, linear x).
- `src/aedist/tabulate_exp1_cost_summary.py` — per-model LaTeX table.
- `experiments/Makefile:220–227` — wires `make exp1-cost-summary` to
  `report/inputs/generated/tab_exp1_cost_summary.tex`.
- `Makefile:145–148` — wires `fig_pareto.pdf` to
  `slides/inputs/generated/`.
- `slides/manuscript/main.md:21–23` — Figure 2 placeholder + stale
  caption ("DeepSeek V3.2 decomposed+RAG @ F1 = 89.8%, $0.06" — pilot
  numbers from a model no longer in the journal lineup).
- `slides/manuscript/main.md` Annex A — currently no cost table.
- PR #375 (already on main) — adds model-family colouring to
  `fig_census_direct`; pattern to copy.

## Actions

Six independently-decidable items. Order them however ships fastest;
do not bundle.

1. **Caption rewrite.** Replace the stale placeholder caption with
   one that matches current Exp 1 data ($2.85 total, F1 ≤ 0.76, no
   Exp 2/3 yet — so the caption stops over-claiming about cost-pushing
   conditions). Concretely: drop "model × method × documentation level,
   Experiments 1–3" until Exp 2/3 land; drop the DeepSeek-V3.2 example
   that no longer exists in the lineup; mark the figure as "Experiment 1
   only" or hide it until Exp 2.
2. **Draw the Pareto envelope.** The caption says "the Pareto-efficient
   frontier is drawn" — make it true. ~10 LoC after sorting points by
   cost ascending and keeping monotonically-increasing F1.
3. **Family colouring.** Lift the model-family colour map from PR #375's
   `plot_census` work into `plot_pareto`. Three families today: EN, FR,
   ZH. Markers stay cloud=○ / local=△ as a second axis.
4. **Log x-axis decision.** Defer to Exp 2/3 (when cost spread crosses
   ~3 orders of magnitude) **or** flip to log10 now for forward-compat.
   Pick one; document the choice in the script docstring.
5. **Cost table in Annex A.** Decide: (a) port
   `tabulate_exp1_cost_summary.py` to also emit a markdown table the
   manuscript `\input`s or pastes into Annex A, or (b) accept that the
   per-model cost table lives only in `report.pdf` and main.md stays
   prose-only on costs ($2.85 total, range across models already in §1
   "Results").
6. **Quality composite axis (deferred).** A real quality-vs-cost
   frontier requires coherence + provenance + temporality scorers,
   which only become measurable once Exp 2/3 land documents. File a
   placeholder follow-up ticket at the end of this work so the
   ambition is durable.

## Test

For each scripted change, the existing `tests/test_plot_pareto.py`
fixture is the entry point; extend with:

- `test_pareto_envelope_monotone` — after the envelope is added, no
  point is strictly above-and-left of the envelope.
- `test_pareto_family_colours` — three families present in the input
  produce three distinct colours; legend reflects them.
- `test_caption_has_no_stale_pilot_numbers` — adherence-style grep on
  `slides/manuscript/main.md`, fails if "DeepSeek V3.2 decomposed+RAG"
  or "89.8%" or "$0.06" appears.

## Verification

- [ ] Action 1: caption matches current data; adherence grep passes.
- [ ] Action 2: envelope visible in the regenerated PDF; test passes.
- [ ] Action 3: family colours visible in the regenerated PDF; legend
  shows EN / FR / ZH (or equivalent labels).
- [ ] Action 4: docstring of `plot_pareto.py` states the chosen axis
